== S: exact identities (q-precision 440)
S1 c7 * c7 = s7 (Cauchy square) for n <= 440: 1
S2 F(t(q)) = theta^2: 1
S3 G(t(q)) = theta: 1
S4 t theta^3 = (eta1 eta7)^3: 1
S5 s^2 = 1 - 26 t - 27 t^2: 1
S6 q dt/dq / t = theta^2 s: 1
S7 s(t) = sqrt(1-26t-27t^2) has integral t-coefficients: 1
S8 s(t(q)) = s(q): 1
S9 theta^6 (1+t)^2 = theta^6 + 2 (eta1 eta7)^3 theta^3 + (eta1 eta7)^6 (holomorphic, weight 6): 1

